+ * Signed data pointers (the __ptrauth qualifier on a field) have to be signed when the image is
+ * loaded: the linker writes them as chained "auth" fixups, which only dyld or Apple's kernelcache
+ * generator can apply, because applying them needs the keys.  This project loads the kernel as a
+ * plain Mach-O with its own loader, which has no keys yet, so on an arm64e build of this tree those
+ * qualifiers are left out and such fields hold plain pointers.  What still is authenticated: return
+ * addresses, indirect calls, function pointers in this file, the pacga thread-state hash, and the
+ * per-process keys the kernel switches to on the way back to EL0 (the EL0/EL1 key switch that
+ * docs/ARM64E.md is about).  A build for Apple silicon would define XNU_PTRAUTH_SIGNED_DATA_PTRS.
+ */
+#if defined(__arm64e__) && !defined(XNU_PTRAUTH_SIGNED_DATA_PTRS)
+#define XNU_PTRAUTH_DATA_PTRS_PLAIN 1
